<b>Taneome
Shizuru</b>

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:35.570
<b>Asabuki
Kogane</b>

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:35.570
<b>Kazuki
Azuma</b>

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:35.570
<b>Ougi
Kinoa</b>

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:35.570
<b>Nono
Hiiragi</b>

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:37.240
<b>Matobai
Shuusaku</b>

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:39.370
<b>Arabashiri
Souya</b>

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:40.820
<b>Tsuwabuki
Akihito</b>

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:42.030
<b>Hazama
Zetsubi</b>

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:43.160
<b>Banryuu
Reoko</b>

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:44.450
<b>Tsuwabuki
Akihito</b>

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:44.450
<b>Matobai
Shuusaku</b>

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:44.450
<b>Banryuu
Reoko</b>

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:44.450
<b>Arabashiri
Souya</b>

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:44.450
<b>Hazama
Zetsubi</b>

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.970
<b><i>Bubuki/Buranki</i></b>

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:42.480
Kinoa!

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:43.800
Hey!

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:51.190
Whoa, now. Bubuki battles are one-on-one—

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:55.570
Hey! The heart isn't supposed to fight!

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:58.470
Are you even listening?

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:01.410
What if that precious heart of yours breaks?

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.320
I don't care about that!

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.120
I'm doing this to protect Kinoa!

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:08.570
Whoops! My foot slipped.

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:11.040
No matter how hard you try,

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.120
as long as I'm not hostile toward you,

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:17.380
that heart will remain 
in Bubuki battle mode.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:23.390
Sheesh! I've never heard of anyone who 
tried to attack with a heart in his hand.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.710
Stop, Azuma.

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:32.210
I'm going to settle things with him.

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:34.710
I have to.

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:37.900
Okay.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:42.740
What? You sure you want to 
give up on helping her?

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:47.160
I might just end up beating the 
little girl with the glasses.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:48.550
Be strong.

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:49.800
Sure...

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:55.710
Hey!

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:57.800
Kogane, Shizuru.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:00.460
We need to get back to the driver's seat.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.720
Now there's no one in our way.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.470
It's finally just the two of us,

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:07.760
Kinoa.

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:10.470
Don't say my name like I'm you're friend!

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:12.560
I'll finish this in one shot!

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:15.520
Great minds think alike!

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:18.320
I was thinking I'd get one
shot in real quick, too!

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.650
Cut the crap, you old lecher!

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:26.890
Gotcha!

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:28.240
Damn you!

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:30.480
I almost wouldn't recognize you.

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:33.370
It's like the girl you were 
when I met you was just a lie.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:38.460
No real man would be so sentimental
for so long over a memory.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:40.520
Well, how could I forget it?

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:43.760
That was our first night 
together, after all.

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:47.210
Their first night together?

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:48.100
What does he mean?

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:51.680
What does he... Don't you even...

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:56.600
Anyway, what the heck happened 
between Kinoa and that cueball?

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:01.200
Quit talking out your ass, you bastard!

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:06.480
Just show us your Bubuki right now!

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:08.160
What are you talking about?

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:09.680
I don't understand.

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.450
Don't play dumb!

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:13.000
We picked up the signal!

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:15.560
Fine, then.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:18.050
You'll talk to us at the station.

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:20.170
P-Please stop!

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:25.200
Don't do that.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:28.180
You need to be gentle with girls.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:29.850
Y-You're...

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.950
Hey, I saved you, and you 
won't even thank me?

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:42.320
I didn't ask for your help.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:45.270
I didn't intend to help you, either.

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:49.530
You should have just asked 
for their help sooner.

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:50.680
Huh?

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:52.280
Are you

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:54.650
a Bubuki user, too?

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:57.160
Yes.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.220
Just so we're clear, I don't have a Bubuki.

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:07.450
Is that so?

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:10.800
Even if I did, I would never use it.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.660
You'd never use it?

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:15.480
Well, why would I use a thing like that?

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:17.180
A thing like that, huh?

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:21.360
Wouldn't they be precious 
mementos from your mom?

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:23.900
Don't just call that a "thing."

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:33.990
Hey!

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:38.350
I told you not to show me stupid crap!

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:39.710
Hey, not bad!

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:41.400
All right!

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:43.710
That Kinoa's not half bad.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:45.300
A-chan! Hii-kun!

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:47.550
Kogane-chan?

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:49.870
What is it? Did something happen?

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:52.840
Horino-san wants you!
She says its an emergency!

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:53.880
What?

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:56.310
Okay.

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:22.440
There's no need to do that.

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:26.250
I'll never forget it, either...

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:36.010
Ah, finally awake, are you, princess?

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:37.930
What is this?!

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:40.170
What is this?! What is this?!

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:42.690
What is this?!

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:46.280
I told myself I wouldn't die 
just lying on the floor,

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:48.700
but in the sky? Never saw that coming.

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:52.450
I guess I should just thank God that 
I get to die with a pretty girl.

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:55.660
The truth is, I'm a government agent.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:59.040
I was investigating corruption 
among the Bubuki police,

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:01.640
but they discovered my identity,

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:03.810
and this is where I ended up.

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:07.040
Sorry you got wrapped up in this.

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:09.630
N-No way...

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:12.130
Government agent, my ass!

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:17.180
Hey, you totally believed it!

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:19.190
That's right, I did!

00:08:19.190 --> 00:08:22.390
I believed every blatant lie you told me!

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:25.020
Sorry about that.

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:26.480
Don't you "sorry" me!

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:30.230
I'll teach you to never toy with 
an innocent maiden's heart!

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:34.090
Now, don't say that.

00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:39.590
Isn't it because you met me that 
you're using your Bubuki right now?

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:43.910
What happened?

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:47.180
An advisory was just announced.

00:08:47.180 --> 00:08:50.590
The Buranki that fell into 
the ocean has awakened.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:53.720
If it continues on its current course,

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:56.800
it should come ashore in 
Kamakura in one hour.

00:08:57.320 --> 00:08:59.820
It's a densely-populated region,

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:01.910
so a lot of damage could be done.

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:05.060
If we keep up this pace, 
we'll encounter the Buranki.

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:07.660
So we should detour around Kama—

00:09:07.660 --> 00:09:09.610
Don't detour. Let's go to Kamakura.

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:12.440
Hey! What are you saying?

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:14.860
Only a Buranki can defeat a Buranki.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:17.160
So we have to go.

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:19.160
What about about the Buranki nest?

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:22.450
We'll go after we take out 
the Buranki in the ocean.

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:26.840
Hiiragi? What's wrong?

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:28.570
"What's wrong"?

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:32.360
Hasn't it crossed your mind 
that we might not beat it?

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:33.010
Nope.

00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:36.200
It's not just that.

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:39.050
Any delay could lead to
more pursuers after us.

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:42.060
Is that any reason to ignore a Buranki?

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:45.060
That settles it, then.

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:47.060
We're heading to Kamakura.

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:49.720
No objections, right, Hiiragi?

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:50.690
Sure.

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:53.440
What's that?

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:55.840
It must be Kino-chan and that guy fighting.

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:56.970
It's trouble.

00:09:56.970 --> 00:09:59.010
There's a problem with the carrier car.

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:00.200
I'm worried about Oubu.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:04.470
No choice, then. We'll go check it out.

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:05.330
Let's go.

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:11.170
<i>The entire city of Kamakura and 
parts of the city of Hayama</i>

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:13.280
<i>are expected to suffer massive damage,</i>

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:16.510
<i>so citizens are advised to evacuate.</i>

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:20.970
<b>Episode 5
Swords and Rings</b>

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:28.400
This is...

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:30.690
Why are those tie-down wires broken?

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:34.190
Must've been a stray shot from 
that Arabashiri bastard.

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:36.080
At this rate, Oubu's gonna fall off.

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:37.490
Leave it to me!

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:47.430
There, got it. That should hold.

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:48.710
Let's head back.

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:50.750
It's hurting.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:51.840
Huh?

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:56.520
A Bubuki weakens the farther away 
it is from its master, right?

00:10:56.520 --> 00:10:59.010
Yeah, that's right. So what?

00:10:59.270 --> 00:11:00.560
Why is that?

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:02.010
Why?

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:06.790
Bubuki are boosters that amplify our Rinzu.

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:08.310
They're just tools.

00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:11.660
Stay here, Hiiragi. Don't leave your Bubuki.

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:14.420
Don't order me around!

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:16.230
Hey! Where are you going?

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:21.820
You can cry like you did 
back then, if you want!

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:23.530
L-Like hell!

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:30.350
Help me! Help me! Help me!

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:34.960
Sorry you got dragged into all this.

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:37.370
You can use this.

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:38.800
It'll replace a parachute.

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:42.550
I wish I could've seen your Bubuki.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:49.480
So long.

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:55.810
<i>Back then, I didn't even 
want to see a Bubuki.</i>

00:11:55.810 --> 00:12:00.970
<i>I knew nothing about them,
yet I inherited two from my mom.</i>

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:03.490
<i>A normal kid wouldn't have things like that.</i>

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:08.000
<i>So I thought if I had things 
like that following me around 24/7,</i>

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:10.500
<i>I'd never be a normal girl.</i>

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:14.670
Hi—

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:16.560
Hi—

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:19.960
Himekiri! Hoemaru!

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:48.480
Hey, these are some nice Bubuki!

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:56.280
And that's how the confused little girl 
Kinoa's heart was set free! Right?

00:12:56.280 --> 00:12:57.710
All thanks to me!

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:00.940
Shut up! No one asked you to do that!

00:13:00.940 --> 00:13:04.040
Even if it was just to 
make me call my Bubuki,

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:05.840
I can't believe you did that.

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:09.470
Well, it was my job.

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:10.660
To determine whether the two swords

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:14.600
comprising the left hand 
of my arch enemy, Oubu,

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:17.610
had been legitimately handed 
down from mother to daughter.

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:22.650
What were you going to do if I 
hadn't called out my Bubuki?

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:24.860
I'd have crossed that 
bridge when I came to it.

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:28.780
Of course, I would've loved to die for you.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:31.990
Bastard! You can't keep
 coming up with lies forever!

00:13:33.770 --> 00:13:36.120
My Iwatooshi is holding it down.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:37.750
Isn't that good enough?

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:40.960
Iwatooshi, hurting?

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:43.560
That's not possible.

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:47.380
Bubuki don't feel pain or joy or anything.

00:13:52.150 --> 00:13:53.770
He's just so irritating...

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:00.980
I don't get you.

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:04.230
Thanks, Hiiragi. You're a big help.

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:14.540
Azuma!

00:14:29.320 --> 00:14:32.350
Why do you hate Bubuki?

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:36.410
Because I'm sure there's 
nothing good about them.

00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:39.210
Since I've had Bubuki forced on me,

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:43.570
I bet the rest of my life 
will be nothing but trouble.

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:45.340
That's not true.

00:14:46.050 --> 00:14:47.860
How can you say that for sure?

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:51.220
You got those two from your mom, right?

00:14:51.220 --> 00:14:56.220
And she got them from her parents, 
and them from theirs, and on and on.

00:14:56.220 --> 00:15:00.120
There's nothing good or bad about something 
handed down for so many generations.

00:15:00.660 --> 00:15:02.990
What you do with them is up to you.

00:15:02.990 --> 00:15:06.200
So you should face your Bubuki head-on.

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:08.460
They're bound to help to you.

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:09.630
Plus...

00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:12.510
They saved my life.

00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:15.040
Treasure them for me.

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:17.830
Of course, you saved my life, too.

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:23.300
Hey, you're pretty cute!

00:15:23.300 --> 00:15:26.150
You can be my girlfriend if you want, Kinoa.

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:45.550
Oops, did I hurt you again?

00:15:45.550 --> 00:15:49.380
I'm sorry. I'll finish you off more gently.

00:15:58.980 --> 00:16:00.640
<i>As long as I'm with you,</i>

00:16:01.490 --> 00:16:05.180
<i>I think I can come to like the Bubuki, too.</i>

00:16:08.710 --> 00:16:10.030
Thanks, Kogane-chan.

00:16:10.480 --> 00:16:11.280
You saved me.

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:14.720
Jeez, don't be so reckless, A-chan.

00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:16.780
Thanks, Righty-chan.

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:20.310
Thanks for protecting Oubu.

00:16:20.310 --> 00:16:23.080
Why are you thanking the Bubuki?

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:25.130
These things are just tools.

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:28.060
Bubuki need us.

00:16:28.060 --> 00:16:28.880
What?

00:16:29.370 --> 00:16:32.480
They weaken the farther 
away we are from them,

00:16:32.480 --> 00:16:35.090
and the more we're with them, 
the stronger they are.

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:38.600
I think Bubuki want to be with 
their users all the time.

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:42.480
Are you <i>serious</i> about that?

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:47.230
"I'm so lonely! I can't use 
my powers without my master!"

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:50.170
Are you saying that's what they think?

00:16:50.170 --> 00:16:51.920
Yeah, I'm sure of it.

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:53.010
What?

00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:55.110
I agree with A-chan!

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:59.020
I believe Righty-chan wants to be with me.

00:16:59.960 --> 00:17:03.330
You're talking about it like
it's a puppy that follows its owner around.

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:05.420
Bubuki aren't animals.

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:06.560
Huh?

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:08.090
They aren't just tools, either.

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:10.640
What are they, then?

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:12.920
I'm not sure myself.

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:14.950
Are you trying to be funny?!

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:18.960
You're Iwatooshi's master, right?

00:17:19.440 --> 00:17:24.380
Then I bet you understand 
Iwatooshi better than anyone.

00:17:25.840 --> 00:17:28.810
You talk like you know it all.

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:31.030
Damn, you piss me off!

00:17:31.030 --> 00:17:32.470
Seriously...

00:17:32.470 --> 00:17:34.420
What the hell is with you?

00:17:36.380 --> 00:17:37.900
The Buranki nest?

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:41.870
Yeah. They say that's where Bubuki are born.

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:44.750
You say you won't accept your Bubuki,

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:48.130
but how much do you even know about them?

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:51.290
I want to know more about Bubuki.

00:17:51.290 --> 00:17:56.040
And I want to see the place where 
they start out with my own eyes.

00:17:56.710 --> 00:18:01.440
Want to have a race to see who makes 
it to the Buranki nest first?

00:18:07.260 --> 00:18:12.980
Looks like you're completely caught up 
in your memories of back then, Kinoa!

00:18:13.590 --> 00:18:19.240
Don't worry, you two.
I won't kill your precious master.

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:24.600
But in return, I'll be your new 
master from this day onward.

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:27.790
That's a good girl, Kinoa.

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:31.160
I'll make this quick,
so just have a little nap there.

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:37.590
What?

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:43.350
The Bubuki attacked its own 
master to wake her up?!

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:53.160
Can I ask you something, Arabashiri?

00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:57.740
Why did you show up now, after all this time?

00:18:57.740 --> 00:19:01.650
Because I wanted to see you again, of co—

00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:03.020
Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:19:03.020 --> 00:19:06.550
I'll tell you! I'll tell you! 
I'll tell you the truth!

00:19:07.390 --> 00:19:10.180
Because Oubu's heart appeared.

00:19:10.180 --> 00:19:12.480
And now that the Bubuki battle has started,

00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:17.140
I can take those two Bubuki from you!

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:19.830
Of course, even back then...

00:19:19.830 --> 00:19:24.740
I may not have taken your Bubuki,
but I managed to take something else!

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:27.520
You really are scum.

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:30.020
Thanks. I'm awake now.

00:19:30.360 --> 00:19:31.940
Hoemaru!

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:34.210
If this had ended while I 
was stuck in that dream,

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:36.440
you would've looked so damned good.

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:52.330
I picked this up at a garbage dump ages ago.

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:53.420
Huh?

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:55.630
I wasn't being serious, you idiot.

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:58.990
That scumbag forced me to take it ages ago.

00:19:59.400 --> 00:20:01.240
I'll go to Treasure Island with you.

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:01.720
Huh?

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:03.760
The place where these two,

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:05.720
Himekiri and Hoemaru, were born...

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:08.500
I'm going to see it

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:10.340
with my own eyes.

00:20:10.340 --> 00:20:12.230
Oh, that's right...

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:16.270
It's where you were born, too, isn't it?

00:20:16.270 --> 00:20:17.240
Weird.

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:19.450
Weird? What's weird about it?

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:21.000
All of it's weird!

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:23.740
You grew up on an island in the sky!

00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:28.740
My goodness, that Arabashiri is so pathetic.

00:20:29.480 --> 00:20:30.500
That's...

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:33.520
Hang in there, Shizuru-chan! What's wrong?!

00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:35.670
Hey, Shizuru! What happened?

00:20:37.060 --> 00:20:40.340
Horino-san wasn't Horino-san...

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:41.320
Huh?

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:42.750
What does that mean?

00:20:45.020 --> 00:20:47.010
H-Horino-san?

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:51.450
Sheesh... I know he's better than that.

00:20:51.450 --> 00:20:53.450
That was sort of bland.

00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:55.230
Maybe he's just a lolicon.

00:20:55.640 --> 00:20:57.040
Hey!

00:20:57.040 --> 00:20:58.230
What are you doing?!

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:02.170
What am I doing? Hmm... 
Cleaning up the trash?

00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:05.340
Waste treatment? Pest extermination?

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:06.930
The point is...

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:09.950
I just can't <i>stand</i> delinquents.

00:21:10.390 --> 00:21:13.960
Are you really Horino-san?

00:21:13.960 --> 00:21:18.130
Sure I am. But Horino is 
just a borrowed identity.

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:20.460
My real name is...

00:21:24.450 --> 00:21:27.970
Zetsubi. Hazama Zetsubi!

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:34.030
One of Reoko-sama's Four Gods, 
like Arabashiri and Matobai.

00:21:36.160 --> 00:21:38.270
No way... You're a liar!

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:43.200
If that's true, why did you tell 
us how to get to the Buranki nest?

00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:47.160
Why did you work with us to come 
up with a plan to get Oubu back?

00:21:47.600 --> 00:21:49.660
Why? Why?!

00:21:50.110 --> 00:21:51.320
Why?!

00:21:51.320 --> 00:21:52.570
Hmm...

00:21:53.010 --> 00:21:54.290
To kill time?

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:56.460
Damn you!

00:21:58.840 --> 00:22:00.080
What is...

00:22:00.710 --> 00:22:04.470
The Bubuki battle between the two left feet

00:22:04.960 --> 00:22:06.430
begins now!
